pipa: touch axes to the real glass spans (1771x2875)

sweet_touch.c clamped raw touch coordinates to TOUCH_ABS_X/Y = 1080x2400
(the alioth glass). The pipa glass spans x 16..1771, y 52..2875 (measured,
see 0187), so every touch past 1080x2400 was clamped away and only the
top-left corner of the glass was usable.

SweetHID.cpp normalized X against 1080 as well; divide by the real pipa
glass width (1771) instead, matching the measured span. The 0187 piecewise
Y stays as is (it was measured on this glass).

---
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
@@ -93,3 +93,3 @@
 #define TOUCH_MAX_FINGERS    10
-#define TOUCH_ABS_X          1080
-#define TOUCH_ABS_Y          2400
+#define TOUCH_ABS_X          1772
+#define TOUCH_ABS_Y          2876
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp
@@ -492,3 +492,3 @@
-		nx = (IOFixed)(((int64_t)x << 16) / 1080);
+		nx = (IOFixed)(((int64_t)x << 16) / 1771);
 		ny = (IOFixed)((ly << 16) / fLogicalH);
 	}
